-- title:
--   Potential-table certificate data, intervals 256–319
-- statement:
--   The concrete rational data for the 64 consecutive intervals numbered 256 through 319 in the 684-cell potential certificate. The records contain the component log bounds, root enclosures, external-field bounds, and interval positions, arranged as a balanced finite table.
--
--   The associated validity theorem checks these data by exact rational arithmetic. Together with the generic soundness theorem, it certifies the potential inequality over this portion of the short segment.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The module and its dependencies import no Mathlib modules.
-- source:
--   Derived rational-certificate encoding of mo271/Zeta5 at commit 7fe736760f4b96bfdb4334b68e3b3124ecbe10b0, Apery/Table2/All.lean, potential_ineq_le_two (lines 4116–4120), and the U*.lean/I*.lean certificate files; https://github.com/mo271/Zeta5/blob/7fe736760f4b96bfdb4334b68e3b3124ecbe10b0/Apery/Table2/All.lean#L4116-L4120. The certificate datatype and its generic soundness adapter are new formalization infrastructure.

